'''Selected quotations''' are drawn from surviving accounts of Ivo Ren. Attribution is given by scene where known; some lines are disputed because revisions changed their witnesses.

== To ordinary people ==

<blockquote>"We can sit until the rain stops. I am poor at stopping rain without changing where it falls." — at a flooded shelter</blockquote>

<blockquote>"Eat first," Teren told him. "You can be unbearable on an empty stomach." Ivo later repeated it to a child preparing to confront a god. — Teren's river notes</blockquote>

== To rulers and enemies ==

<blockquote>"You may own every answer in this room. I am asking who locked the door." — to a cosmic tyrant</blockquote>

<blockquote>"Within this account, there is nothing you cannot do." — to [[The Closed King]]</blockquote>

== On descriptions ==

<blockquote>"I thought that was the sky. It seems to be a sentence about one." — on discovering a second account</blockquote>

<blockquote>"A correction is an event. I forgot that when I was young." — after the evacuation bell</blockquote>

== On identity ==

<blockquote>"Mira laughed at the cup. Or I have told myself so often that the laugh learned to sound like hers." — on [[The Anchor Memory]]</blockquote>

<blockquote>"Tell me what you chose when no one would know." — to another Ivo</blockquote>

== On power ==

<blockquote>"Then you have missed several people I could not save." — when called omnipotent</blockquote>

<blockquote>"Ask someone whose life I changed without permission. You may get a better answer." — when asked whether he is God</blockquote>

<blockquote>"A good reason to leave a thing broken. I have lost to those before." — when asked what could defeat him</blockquote>

== The Author Event ==

<blockquote>"Every rebellion you ever performed was something I wrote." — the apparent Author</blockquote>

<blockquote>"Then who wrote your certainty?" — Ivo Ren</blockquote>

The Author Event has incompatible surviving versions. The lines are common to them, but the exchange's outcome is not settled. See [[Sovereign/History]].

